  "details": "IVRCImageDownload objects have a \"Progress\" property that returns a float to indicate the download progress. IVRCStringDownload on the other hand does not, in spite of being the functional equivalent object for strings. When the user has a slow connection and/or for larger strings, this provides no way for the world (and thus the player in turn) to know if anything is actually happening.\n\nFor even greater feature parity, the \"State\" property would also be nice to add, which currently exists to indicate the state of a loading image (VRCImageDownloadState), but has no equivalent for loading strings.",
